  "term": "intermarriage",
  "definition": "In this historical source, intermarriage means marriage within a group sharing a condition or family connection, especially marriages between deaf people or between blood relatives. It is discussed as a supposed factor in congenital deaf-dumbness, though the passage also questions giving too much weight to marriage between relatives alone.",
